35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found the northern roads closed eleven days, yet local halls kept their evening schedules. Also, outreach averaged forty visitors, beating our midweek numbers.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The bus cuts are severe. An hour’s round trip isolates those wards. Yet remote catalogue peaks after nine, when we lock up.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, forty visitors is huge! But the digitisation project failed badly. We can’t just copy old mistakes. We need to know why it broke.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The grant covers sessions for a year, then the flat budget absorbs the cost. That’s the trap. We’re borrowing from year two to fund year one.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The register shows retired tradespeople running clinics, but no paid staff supervise them. The tool technician retired. We lack the necessary oversight skills.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, I hear your caution. The halls kept their own timetables despite the closures, which suggests local resilience. We must build on that stability, not guess.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, that funding trap is real. But the access gap is immediate. We can’t wait for year two to fix who can reach us now.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, the grant trap is scary! But those evening groups survived without help. Why did the photos fail? We need to fix the process, not just the money!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, the access gap is real, but if the funding structure collapses in year two, we’re just building a house on sand.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the funding trap is real, but our staffing gap is immediate. We cannot supervise new programs without trained staff.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, I understand your worry about supervision. But those halls proved people can manage themselves. Perhaps we need fewer, steadier steps rather than rushing into complex new roles.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, supervision is vital. Yet if we lock doors at nine while demand peaks later, we fail the very people we aim to serve.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the evening groups proved people can self-manage! We don’t need paid supervisors for everything. Let’s trust the community’s existing energy!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, supervision is a cost, not a virtue. If the grant vanishes, we can’t afford the luxury of trained staff. We need a model that survives the budget cut.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, self-management is not supervision. We lack certified technicians and trained supervisors. We cannot assign new duties without verifying the skills exist on our roster.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I find comfort in those steady halls. Let us choose a path that does not depend on weather or shifting grants.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We must respect the quiet hours. Let’s find a way to serve those late-night users without disrupting the peace we cherish.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I’m done! The old records proved my point. We have the data to make a smart choice, not just a lucky guess.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I’m done. The ledger confirms my fear: we overspend on operations and underspend on assets. We need a proposal that respects that structural imbalance.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,I stand by my findings. We lack the certified skills to safely manage new tools. We must verify capabilities before expanding.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
