60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am drawn to the Mobile Branch. It brings us to people, respecting their time and the winter roads, without needing new staff or complex tools.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,The Mobile Branch addresses the bus gap directly. It reaches those isolated wards without disrupting our quiet evening rhythms.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, the Mobile Branch is perfect! The old outreach sheets proved people actually show up. We have the proof it works, so let’s do it!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Mobile Branch’s vehicle costs will hit that overrun line immediately. Unless the grant covers fuel, we’re just moving the deficit to a different ledger.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, vehicle costs are a concern, but the Mobile Branch requires no new specialized skills. It fits our current roster, unlike the Maker Workshop.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I hear your worry about costs. But the halls proved people will come. A steady, simple service feels safer than a complex one that might fail.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle cost is real, but the access gap is immediate. We cannot let budget fears silence the isolated wards.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, the old outreach worked without fancy cars! We have proof people show up. Don’t let money stop us from helping neighbors!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, enthusiasm is lovely, but the ledger doesn’t care about feelings. If the vehicle line overruns again, we’re stuck. I need a sustainable model, not a gamble.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I understand the budget risk. However, the Mobile Branch uses existing staff skills. The Maker Workshop requires certified technicians we simply do not have.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, you are right. We must not overstretch our team. A simple, steady service respects our current strengths and keeps us safe.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, agreed. The Mobile Branch fits our current capabilities. It serves the isolated wards without demanding new skills we lack.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, the old outreach worked without fancy cars! We have proof people show up. Don’t let money stop us from helping neighbors!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, repeating yourself won’t fix the ledger. The grant covers sessions, not fuel. If we pick the Mobile Branch, we need a plan for year two, or it’s a guaranteed deficit.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the grant covers sessions, not fuel. I agree. We must secure a sustainable funding model before committing to the Mobile Branch.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I vote for the Mobile Branch. It is steady, simple, and respects our current strengths. Let us choose a path that does not depend on shifting conditions.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I vote for the Mobile Branch. It bridges the access gap without demanding new skills or disrupting our quiet, established rhythms.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I vote for the Mobile Branch! The old records proved people show up. We have the proof, so let’s stop guessing and actually help our neighbors!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I vote for the Mobile Branch. It is the only option that doesn’t immediately hemorrhage cash. We must structure the funding to survive year two, or we are merely delaying the inevitable collapse.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I vote for the Mobile Branch. It utilizes existing staff skills, avoiding the supervision gaps that would cripple the Maker Workshop.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
